me": "Milad Irannejad", "email": "mirannejad@gitlab.com", "date": "2024-10-15T22:12:07Z"}, "message": "Add ai-abstraction-layer Sidekiq shard", "tree": {"sha": "e0a801cad330ad50fbcea287460eb5e2c67dda40", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mattrussi/gitlab-com-runbooks/git/trees/e0a801cad330ad50fbcea287460eb5e2c67dda40"}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mattrussi/gitlab-com-runbooks/git/commits/c5f569faf46625e24271543bbe033ce5be48149d", "comment_count": 0, "verification": {"verified": false, "reason": "unsigned", "signature": null, "payload": null, "verified_at": null}}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mattrussi/gitlab-com-runbooks/commits/c5f569faf46625e24271543bbe033ce5be48149d", "html_url": "https://github.com/mattrussi/gitlab-com-runbooks/commit/c5f569faf46625e24271543bbe033ce5be48149d", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mattrussi/gitlab-com-runbooks/commits/c5f569faf46625e24271543bbe033ce5be48149d/comments", "author": null, "committer": null, "parents": [{"sha": "110ed3e66b1f3beb0921e4692990763b286b1b02", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mattrussi/gitlab-com-runbooks/commits/110ed3e66b1f3beb0921e4692990763b286b1b02", "html_url": "https://github.com/mattrussi/gitlab-com-runbooks/commit/110ed3e66b1f3beb0921e4692990763b286b1b02"}]}, {"sha": "8a4bcfc1dafa8be2fc30a8d4c7d22a4d570c9bff", "node_id": "C_kwDOOUG3R9oAKDhhNGJjZmMxZGFmYThiZTJmYzMwYThkNGM3ZDIyYTRkNTcwYzliZmY", "commit": {"author": {"name": "Bob Van Landuyt", "email": "bob@gitlab.com", "date": "2024-08-12T08:27:04Z"}, "committer": {"name": "Bob Van Landuyt", "email": "bob@gitlab.com", "date": "2024-08-12T08:27:04Z"}, "message": "fix: avoid patchy kube_container_cpu metrics\n\nWe monitor `kube_container_cpu` for all containers that don't have a\nlimit configured. We do this by checking if the\n`container_spec_cpu_quota` metric exists and hide the utilization if\nit does.\n\n`container_spec_cpu_quota` is exported per pod, and then recorded into\na `container_spec_cpu_quota:labeled` to be used in other recording\nrules.\n\nBecause the pods come and go, and both\n`container_spec_cpu_quota:labeled` and\n`container_cpu_usage_seconds_total:labeled` go through recording\nrules. We might have one available later than the other. At this\nmoment we'd record one of the \"patches\" for the saturation metric that\nwe actually wanted to hide.\n\nWe can work around this by using a `last_over_time` for\n`container_spec_cpu_quota:labeled`.\n\nFor https://gitlab.com/gitlab-com/gl-infra/scalability/-/issues/3724", "tree": {"sha": "1911bf1523e75fb29a474ee1b65ed3f1d62122ed", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mattrussi/gitlab-com-runbooks/git/trees/1911bf1523e75fb29a474ee1b65ed3f1d62122ed"}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mattrussi/gitlab-com-runbooks/git/commits/8a4bcfc1dafa8be2fc30a8d4c7d22a4d570c9bff", "comment_count": 0, "verification": {"verified": false, "reason": "unknown_key", "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAAhcAAAAHc3NoLXJzYQAAAAMBAAEAAAIBAMkmSqe9GoYGn3EVX7/d0b\n3lzHbPiZrygfAxSd5r1zCcgGm+o7FK6Rd2+3+exf+xGW59/JH2wyYXVIkk6J+MpZrEesAF\nZaaCg9pSsBfLCpdeKIHNcbSq3weSRjep67KL7VLnufY6x4HeUMCoyeBQOVcg/qNXWAni8g\nvgBwHBzj8hOkKJXA8tdkcgT8ELP2mbrSy6mNkIgnkqnEYHOlpHWOGkXxBmLdS4bxtRK76r\nGuKA4foFcgewpEP5vbSYLCpruGG5s+Kt7pgjs91ktOXCtHg5yJKIg/S3bgSfxAQQUdJ1dW\nFiz7FKtsTMYHY5a21AdDzSYCvp5n3gKbxkeOw+48Eg5v9v5TZ7T1OhmxULDJAOleCRmHSS\neEsjMnHgaRjFWyhi/rzPBOqO0S2zpqq7TN/Wkb4rRNlkLkaIuTxFbYz5OGuVuV/rqm9A2z\nBLg3zYJloGAUA39BSrB70899YWuTE4KR3hepIvXwanhmco/Hogqcs9Wwovm/oYC1RABhxd\nWVLoEMcOAHMvBTUrK4QCVAGNU+0Pdl/lOhpxhQ0ccAOOXfjcwB9kcNjIMi2mW3q8Rh/C/k\nNo2fmlMK5QNdlJbkoADNolJwkMXUog9xhh7dfloSWes6wzg/zDxiJObdI0/FRpsveR2mzn\nTMEKi1K6lM3jEp2obDuSXqkYLAlp2MajAAAAA2dpdAAAAAAAAAAGc2hhNTEyAAACFAAAAA\nxyc2Etc2hhMi0yNTYAAAIAFboOalCsWe4FAe7FPcXUycguKSNRUHgGOo12869janY2L8b1\npzrBIEphS9ArADppVHAZMu1Gh0qmAqgJfQsRjWK59Hr4wiKU1a8Q73UamYHk4adiNwRyfr\nbWODX/SnvK4uM9ntRz35bQ9XFPiSajvhYwiq6DlKaDNFHgQxKljdedn7R2R+kYIr3D1UAe\nbtl9QXSx3+JBpInHFV9BnSkNTdbKLJph7QdqqQSdgRVWaZRPiTrlNZxGNGWLltGC/mPvWp\n7TeZQPM/JSaIoN65zmeWP6k2uvfcG0Du3bG7t0eg80fq36E8QEekET6Y+QGBknT8+3/53z\noTmq5qbVkMm9Sw/VQr8v8HSV+352PerkXN7a0TysL49aIw3c74wtZocABKQ2WEMjHmXm59\nnZfvqgjRSd9HWAJCljB3apcxWUpMftGD0WaS9HUpv/MynGeuaVWFMV0Yj8OG6S9j+ScjYW\n2Tq1OIJBGqwzA4s2K5tZt4y92+hNo8J/6pSAxWuGAkKBJAJTcF1e8VZPbA7Ydk8gS9/bW1\nmY0m7Io/wtnyXKauzovZcg5Hy/Fe0bJi8Txm8mBWxyII4oo9ytQ/IfnLU0F6xocUe3cPxs\nUr3yyH9LBfPgiad8NUgtZgZQ4muUJxCzh5F3NQBkq3jDNcl9B6J1lMmPZkCS9y1HsZKbks\nSN7nk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----", "payload": "tree 1911bf1523e75fb29a474ee1b65ed3f1d62122ed\nparent dba5801457178d1ff40fba3c2e1960f9337e5a73\nauthor Bob Van Landuyt <bob@gitlab.com> 1723451224 +0200\ncommitter Bob Van Landuyt <bob@gitlab.com> 1723451224 +0200\n\nfix: avoid patchy kube_container_cpu metrics\n\nWe monitor `kube_container_cpu` for all containers that don't have a\nlimit configured. We do this by checking if the\n`container_spec_cpu_quota` metric exists and hide the utilization if\nit does.\n\n`container_spec_cpu_quota` is exported per pod, and then recorded into\na `container_spec_cpu_quota:labeled` to be used in other recording\nrules.\n\nBecause the pods come and go, and both\n`container_spec_cpu_quota:labeled` and\n`container_cpu_usage_seconds_total:labeled` go through recording\nrules. We might have one available later than the other. At this\nmoment we'd record one of the \"patches\" for the saturation metric that\nwe actually wanted to hide.\n\nWe can work around this by using a `last_over_time` for\n`container_spec_cpu_quota:labeled`.\n\nFor https://gitlab.com/gitlab-com/gl-infra/scalability/-/issues/3724\n", "verified_at": null}}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mattrussi/gitlab-com-runbooks/commits/8a4bcfc1dafa8be2fc30a8d4c7d22a4d570c9bff", "html_url": "https://github.com/mattrussi/gitlab-com-runbooks/commit/8a4bcfc1dafa8be2fc30a8d4c7d22a4d570c9bff", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mattrussi/gitlab-com-runbooks/commits/8a4bcfc1dafa8be2fc30a8d4c7d22a4d570c9bff/commen